{:edb/db-before-t 2033 :edb/db-after-t 2034 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535346 50 #inst "2026-10-08T22:30:27.267Z" 13194139535346 true] [17592186195309 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345092 13194139535346 true] [17592186195309 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345092 13194139535346 true] [17592186195310 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345093 13194139535346 true] [17592186195310 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345093 13194139535346 true] [17592186195311 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345094 13194139535346 true] [17592186195311 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345094 13194139535346 true] [17592186198402 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345152 13194139535346 true] [17592186198403 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345095 13194139535346 true] [17592186198403 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345114 13194139535346 true] [17592186198403 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345133 13194139535346 true] [17592186198717 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535346 true] [17592186198717 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063256/assets/fbd778f48199acd5b731e739cb527a990ba28a8d88981d50554d135e853f8815.png)\n\nUse set builder notation to describe the shaded region given in the diagram above:\n\n${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n${x}^{2}\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n${y}^{2}$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$36$\n\n$}$" 13194139535346 true] [17592186198717 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4392/Source/Images/q-181610.png)\n\nUse set builder notation to describe the shaded region given in the diagram above:${(x, y) ∈ R^{2}$:\n{{field-1}}\n$x^{2} +$\n{{field-2}}\n$y^{2}$\n{{field-3}}\n$36$\n$}$" 13194139535346 false] [17592186198717 1145 "The equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the elliptical boundary of our region has horizontal radius $a=3$ and vertical radius $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can write as\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=36.\n$$\n\nWe're interested in describing all points that lie *inside* the ellipse. So, let's pick any point inside the region, say, $(0,0).$ Substituting its coordinates into the equation of the boundary, we obtain\n\n$$\n4(0)^{2}+9(0)^{2}\\,<\\,36.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the points $P(x,y)$ in our region are any real numbers that satisfy the condition\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}<36.\n$$\n\nNotice that we use $<$ since the boundary is excluded from the set (the boundary curve is dashed).\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}<36}.\n$$" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345092 1034 "4" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345092 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535346 true] [17592186345092 1111 #uuid "51f32536-8553-5777-bd2f-2bc5fde22ae9" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345093 1034 "9" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345093 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535346 true] [17592186345093 1111 #uuid "ca2c3569-8e4d-568d-a6c0-54b175067ab2" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345094 1034 "<" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345094 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535346 true] [17592186345094 1111 #uuid "3b910099-c567-5648-8f68-a3d99b4db76a" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345095 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345096 13194139535346 true] [17592186345095 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345102 13194139535346 true] [17592186345095 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345108 13194139535346 true] [17592186345095 1089 "q-181687" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345095 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535346 true] [17592186345095 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063256/assets/f6a3b3bc0064525271804e6d20689c21ca84c0adad138a8bd8d398be66e45c3e.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,-x-1\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,x+2}\n$$" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345095 1113 #uuid "f12574d2-ca01-52cd-b44a-2021e52b83d2" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345095 1145 "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-x-1$ and *below* the line $y=x+2.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-x-1,\\,y<x+2.\n$$\n\n \n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n-x-1<y<x+2\n$$\n\nSince the boundary is not included in the set (the lines are dashed), the inequalities are strict.\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-x-1<y<x+2}.\n$$" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345096 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345097 13194139535346 true] [17592186345096 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345098 13194139535346 true] [17592186345096 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345099 13194139535346 true] [17592186345096 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345100 13194139535346 true] [17592186345096 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345101 13194139535346 true] [17592186345096 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535346 true] [17592186345096 1041 "field-1" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345096 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345097 13194139535346 true] [17592186345096 1110 #uuid "0eb374c7-b3c4-5538-879b-ca3d3d4fbb1c" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345097 1034 "{R}^{2}" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345097 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535346 true] [17592186345097 1111 #uuid "2c088c2b-a005-57fb-ba1f-103fa4afad25" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345098 1034 "N" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345098 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535346 true] [17592186345098 1111 #uuid "60512c4c-8ffa-5213-9bfa-767c50d061a5" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345099 1034 "C" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345099 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535346 true] [17592186345099 1111 #uuid "47ef57eb-5324-53fd-9e76-f2377acc0b5b" 13194139535346 true] [17592186345100 1034 "{C}^{2}" 131941395353